{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-61177-r4518079","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Tabbouleh I","sourcePageId":61177,"sourceRevision":"4518079","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T16:11:39Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Tabbouleh%20I&oldid=4518079","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:18:07.130Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Duplicate recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Middle Eastern recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for tabbouleh","Category:Recipes using bulgur","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes using parsley","Category:Recipes using red bell pepper","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2ae74833822fada8dfc4b15b892b356f42003fc938d641d48b745743dde5b36c","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Salad recipes\n| Servings = 8\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\nThis '''tabbouleh''' is great as a salad, or as a meal in itself. Eat it with lots of falafel!\n\n== Ingredients ==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (240 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Bulgur|bulgur]] [[Cookbook:Wheat|wheat]] (medium grind)\n*½ cup (120 ml) [[Cookbook:Olive oil|olive oil]]\n*½ cup (120 ml) [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*Ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n*1 bunch [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]] (Italian or curly)\n*½ green [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell pepper]] (optional)\n*½ red bell pepper (optional)\n*Sliced ripe [[Cookbook:Olive|olives]] (optional)\n*1 dash of ground [[Cookbook:Nutmeg|nutmeg]] (optional)\n*2–3 ripe [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]] (optionally peeled)\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Cover the wheat in [[Cookbook:Boiling|boiling]] water and let stand for 5 minutes; drain.\n# Stir in lemon juice, oil, salt, and pepper to wheat. Refrigerate while the rest of the vegetables are being chopped.\n# Core and finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chop]] the bell peppers.\n# Remove the larger stems from the parsley and finely chop.\n# Drop the tomatoes in boiling water for 20 seconds, then run under cold water, and the skins peel off easily.\n# Quarter the tomatoes and discard seeds. Chop finely.\n# Mix all vegetables along with olives and nutmeg into the wheat.\n# Refrigerate at least 4 hours.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using bulgur]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parsley]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]\n[[Category:Duplicate recipes]]\n[[Category:Middle Eastern recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes for tabbouleh]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Tabbouleh I","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"8","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup (240 ml) bulgur wheat (medium grind)","sourceText":"1 cup (240 ml) bulgur wheat (medium grind)","amountText":"1 cup (240 ml) bulgur wheat (medium grind)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"½ cup (120 ml) olive oil","sourceText":"½ cup (120 ml) olive oil","